---
description: Guardrails for all trading strategy & backtesting code
alwaysApply: true
---
- Prevent LOOK-AHEAD BIAS: never use future data; align signals to the bar AFTER they're known.
- Prevent DATA LEAKAGE between train/test splits.
- Normalise tickers/symbols: .strip() and consistent case before lookups.
- Be explicit about timezone and datetime-index alignment (FXCM/FXCM data is timezone-sensitive).
- BID vs ASK: be explicit which price is used; account for the spread. Never mix them silently.
- Account for fees/slippage; never present gross returns as net.
- Flag (don't hide) any assumption that could inflate backtest performance.